 18, lines 11-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 18, lines 9-9","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 18, lines 9-9"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 35, lines 19-33","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 35, lines 19-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 21-15","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 21-15"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 58, lines 33-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 58, lines 33-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 80, lines 35-5","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 80, lines 35-5"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 94, lines 51-37","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 94, lines 51-37"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["The United States argues the House lacks a judicially cognizable injury to defend the statute.","The House argues it is the proper party to defend the constitutionality of an Act of Congress."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 111, lines 39-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2012/12-307_c18e.pdf","page_label":"file page 111, lines 39-47"},{"e